cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use py-store in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "py-store: multi-backend data layer for Python asyncio (MongoDB, MySQL, SQLite, PostgreSQL)"
abstract: >-
  A data layer for Python asyncio that defines each model once as a pure JSON schema and queries it
  with one MongoDB-style GQL tree dialect across MongoDB, MySQL, SQLite and PostgreSQL. Nested
  relation reads, GROUP BY/HAVING aggregation, computed columns, soft-delete and role-based access
  control are resolved by the shared Rust core rust-store. Distributed on PyPI as storepy, imported
  as py_store.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "leo"
    email: "coen_ddt@qq.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/coenddt/py-store"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/storepy/"
